  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &1756015215
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1756015214}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51bf743a7b9a61e409329faa416e2f81, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Ronin7.World::Ronin7.World.Story.DialoguePlayer
  lines:
  - speaker: Iris
    text: Cipher. I need you to hear this now, it changes the shape of what you just
      told her. We finished cross-checking the command records against your own Program
      file. They don't match.
    seconds: 12
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f7eff729adbaa344489c2a2b3d4770d2, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Match how.
    seconds: 1
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 330081361676b1b4ca67c41fada9eb8d, type: 3}
  - speaker: Iris
    text: The operative-of-record for this massacre is logged as Kael Vor. The name
      I flagged at the briefing. It still won't resolve, because there's nothing
      under it to resolve to. Nobody misfiled this. They planted it.
    seconds: 15
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 719b68a4af65807499d7746c32b6fd8d, type: 3}
  - speaker: Mera Voss
    text: She's right, and I've seen the trick a hundred times without turning it
      over. We logged kills under cover-names so the count would belong to a man
      who didn't exist. Kael Vor was a coat the Program hung the bodies on.
    seconds: 15
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fff27b8283b99a94190e26bb7fc06dbb, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: So the name they hung this on isn't even mine.
    seconds: 3
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0e3b5d341b1f2f74a80e573080e2396e, type: 3}
  - speaker: Iris
    text: It was never yours, Cipher. Someone printed Kael Vor to carry the blame
      so the hand that did this could be wiped clean and kept.
    seconds: 9
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9913aa2d64a10b24f8df0c1e251f1b2e, type: 3}
  - speaker: Echo
    text: I carried that name behind your eyes for years and logged it as fact. They
      leave you a fake to hold so you never go looking for the real one. We go looking
      now.
    seconds: 11
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1c29ff71df8b07445b85568cf03bc505, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Even the name on it was a lie. They couldn't tell the truth about who killed
      her.
    seconds: 5
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 77ca575089e48ed4cab3ab0869f90ee7, type: 3}
  textMesh: {fileID: 1135153134}
  panelRoot: {fileID: 837809801}
  audioSource: {fileID: 1756015216}
  billboardToCamera: 1
  playOnStart: 0
  followDistance: 1.5
